otop (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Apply Odoo's own defaults for workers (0) and max_cron_threads (2) when
    odoo.conf omits them, instead of treating the worker counts as unknown and
    leaving every child process untyped.
  * Keep per-process CPU baselines and busy history across instances: with more
    than one instance configured, each pass discarded the other instance's
    state, so CPU% and BUSY% never had a previous sample to compare against.
    Cached state is now dropped only when the process itself is gone.

 -- Ahmed Sajidh <ahmedsajidh@gmail.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 01:30:00 +0000

otop (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial release: terminal monitor for Odoo instances.
    - server metrics: CPU (with per-core), RAM, swap, load, disk I/O, network
    - Odoo worker table with evidence-based busy/idle and a rolling busy share
    - storage: total disk first, then database, filestore and other
    - PostgreSQL: connections, active/idle/waiting, long queries, sizes
    - LIVE / STAGING switching, configuration in /etc/otop/config.yaml

 -- Ahmed Sajidh <ahmedsajidh@gmail.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
